# Starmind (SpaceX orbital data centers): the filed shells of the 29 May 2026 FCC letter, Table 1.
# s10: from 30,000 km over the dusk terminator, the sun-synchronous X-ring alone (two terminator
#      rings, LTAN 18:00 and 06:00, crossing at the equator) — highlighted so the night side shows too.
# s20: the 30 deg shells alone from the same spot (a band to +-30 deg latitude).
# s30: both. s40: the evening sky from 35 N, 30 min after sunset, looking west.
# s50: one cluster up close (10 satellites, 1 km apart along track).
preset High
const list
time set 2037-03-20T00:00:00Z
time pause
observer lat=0 lon=-90 alt=30000000
camera az=90 el=-90 fov=50
const all off
const "SpaceX Starmind - sun-synchronous X-ring" on highlight=on
wait settle
capture s10_xring scale=0.5
const all off
const "SpaceX Starmind - 30 deg shells" on highlight=on
wait settle
capture s20_30deg scale=0.5
const "SpaceX Starmind - sun-synchronous X-ring" on highlight=on
wait settle
capture s30_both scale=0.5
const all on
observer lat=35 lon=-100 agl=2
time sun -7 setting
camera az=270 el=20 fov=90
wait settle
capture s40_evening scale=0.5
state s40_evening
select const "SpaceX Starmind - 30 deg shells"
camera look sel
camera fov=1.5
wait settle
capture s50_cluster scale=0.5
